---
import LegalLayout from "@layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "@data/site";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The terms that govern use of the LeadOrbiq Chrome extension and this website."
  pathname="/terms-of-service/"
  lastUpdated="August 1, 2026"
>
  <p>
    These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your use of the LeadOrbiq Chrome extension and this
    website (together, the "Service"). By installing or using LeadOrbiq, you agree to these Terms.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Description of the Service</h2>
  <p>
    LeadOrbiq is a Chrome extension designed to help users collect and organize business lead
    information while researching prospects, primarily through Google Maps. It is not a standalone
    web application, and it is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Google.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Eligibility</h2>
  <p>
    LeadOrbiq is intended for business and professional use by users capable of forming a binding
    contract in their jurisdiction. You are responsible for ensuring your use of the Service
    complies with laws applicable to you.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>When using LeadOrbiq, you agree to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Comply with applicable privacy, data-protection, and marketing laws.</li>
    <li>Respect Google Maps' and any other third-party platform's terms of use.</li>
    <li>Use collected business information for lawful, legitimate business purposes.</li>
    <li>Identify yourself accurately in any outreach based on collected information.</li>
    <li>Personalize outreach rather than sending unsolicited bulk messages.</li>
    <li>Honor opt-out requests from businesses you contact.</li>
    <li>
      Avoid attempting to disrupt, reverse-engineer, or abuse the Service beyond its intended use.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Your responsibility for collected data</h2>
  <p>
    LeadOrbiq is a research and organization tool. You are solely responsible for how you use any
    business information you collect or organize with it, including compliance with applicable laws
    in your jurisdiction and the jurisdictions of businesses you contact.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Accounts and plans</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>[VERIFY]</strong> Account requirements, plan structures, usage limits, and billing terms have
    not been confirmed for publication yet. Once confirmed, this section and the
    <a href="/pricing/">Pricing page</a> will describe them consistently.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The LeadOrbiq name, logo, and associated branding are the property of LeadOrbiq. This Service
    does not grant you rights to Google Maps or any third-party platform's trademarks, branding, or
    underlying data beyond what those platforms' own terms permit.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Disclaimers</h2>
  <p>
    The Service is provided "as is" and "as available," without warranties of any kind, express or
    implied, including but not limited to accuracy, completeness, or fitness for a particular
    purpose. LeadOrbiq does not guarantee the accuracy of business information sourced from
    third-party platforms such as Google Maps.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent permitted by law, LeadOrbiq will not be liable for indirect, incidental,
    special, consequential, or punitive damages arising from your use of, or inability to use, the
    Service.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Service availability and changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may modify, suspend, or discontinue any part of the Service at any time. We'll aim to
    communicate material changes clearly, including through updates to these Terms.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Termination</h2>
  <p>
    You may stop using LeadOrbiq at any time by uninstalling the extension. We may suspend or
    terminate access to the Service for use that violates these Terms.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>[VERIFY]</strong> The governing jurisdiction for these Terms has not been confirmed yet.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Changes to these Terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these Terms as the Service evolves. Continued use of LeadOrbiq after changes take
    effect constitutes acceptance of the revised Terms.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these Terms can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.supportEmail}`}
      >{siteConfig.supportEmail}</a
    >
    or through the <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
